      ],
      "source": "https://chenangohistorical.org/town/smithville/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The original Genegantslet Roller Mills, built in 1809 by Nicholas Powell, used a waterwheel powered by a dam on Genegantslet Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://chenangohistorical.org/town/smithville/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Frederick Hansmann bought the mill in 1912 and invented a pancake mix that only required water, the first of its kind.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://chenangohistorical.org/town/smithville/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Tarbell Farms, once the largest producer of Guernsey milk in the Northeast, ran over 3,300 acres and shipped milk by rail to New York City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://chenangohistorical.org/town/smithville/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1961 the Tarbells raised more than 500 purebred Guernsey cattle, plus horses, swine, sheep and chickens.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://chenangohistorical.org/town/smithville/"
    },
    {
